      "verdict": {
        "achieved": false,
        "reason": "All three inputs encode MALK*. The baseline (first input) scores 2055.1996 under OSTIR with the same UTR and settings, via score_base. The 35 synonymous mutants all passed the protein and length gates. beats_reference then kept 16 mutants, each scoring 2139 to 2830, strictly above the baseline. The mutant with exactly 2055.1996 was sent to the no branch, so equal-to-baseline was excluded. The outcome therefore matches the expected result. Coverage is incomplete: valid_dna_output also requires the reading frame, start codon and stop codon to be preserved, and only length and the DNA type are asserted. No assertion checks the stop codon directly. Several variants end in TAG or TGA where the first input has TAA. I only confirmed by eye that these are still stops, and the protein_gate assertion does not say whether it compares the stop. The protein check also uses the first input as the sole reference, which is harmless only because every input encodes the same protein. The protein_preserved, higher_initiation_rate and only_improved_kept criteria are covered by the protein gate and the strict beats_reference bar.\n\nAcceptance: the verifier judged the assertions not to cover the goal",
        "agrees": true,
        "covers_goal": false
      },
      "critique": {
        "diagnosis": "The pipeline did what the goal asked, but the plan cannot prove the valid_dna_output criterion. mutate_synonymous made 35 variants, and all passed protein_gate and length_gate. score_base gave the first input a baseline of 2055.1996, and beats_reference kept 16 variants scoring 2139 to 2830. The variant scoring exactly 2055.1996 went to the no branch, so the strict bar held. The remaining gap is that no step checks that the start and stop codons are preserved. Several variants end in TAG or TGA where the first input ends in TAA, and nothing documents whether protein_unchanged compares the stop.",
        "root_cause": "missing_tool",
        "evidence": [
          "The inputs encode MALK*, but constraint_check reports only protein_unchanged, length_unchanged, targets_remaining and targets_unreachable. Its description does not say whether the stop is compared, and it has no start or stop codon score.",
          "The valid_dna_output assertion is attached to length_gate.yes, which only checks length. Frame, start codon and stop codon are not asserted by any step.",
          "Kept variants such as ATGGCGCTTAAATAG (TAG), ATGGCATTAAAATGA (TGA) and ATGGCACTCAAATAA (TAA) show the stop codon varies across variants, and nothing confirms each one is still a stop.",
          "The first-codon check is only implicit: OSTIR scores a non-ATG start as 0, and every kept variant scores above 2000, so no variant has lost its ATG start."
        ],
        "keep": [
          "score_base",
          "mutants",
          "check",
          "protein_gate",
          "length_gate",
          "score_mut",
          "improved",
          "improved_check"
        ],
        "fix": "Request a new node that checks start and stop codon integrity, for example 'terminal_codons_check'. It should compare each recoded sequence with its reference and report start_codon_unchanged (first codon is ATG) and stop_is_valid (last in-frame codon is TAA, TAG or TGA, with no premature in-frame stop). Once it exists, add it after length_gate with an at_least gate at 1.0 and attach the valid_dna_output assertion to its yes branch. Keep the rest of the wiring: mutants, check, protein_gate, length_gate, score_base and score_mut feeding beats_reference."
      },
